#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Enforce feature-flag registry and flag-bead integrity.

Static rules (also run under ``just validate``, no bead store required):

1. every definition names its flag bead
2. the generated ``feature_flags`` schema block matches the registry
3. every registered key has at least one non-test reference
4. no flag is resolved at module import time
5. no repo-managed config layer overrides an unregistered ``feature_flags``
   key

Bead-status rules (``just lint``, via ``BD_COMMAND``):

6. the named bead exists, is a ``flag`` task bead (or a legacy flag
   issue-type bead), and its key (and kind, when present) match
7. a closed flag bead whose definition survives is an error
8. a live flag bead with no definition is an error, unless the bead is
   newer than this checkout (or still inside the landing grace), in
   which case it is a warning for another tree's in-flight ``sase flag
   new``
9. an overdue flag is a warning, never an error

A future ``_lint-backcompat`` recipe should register another
:class:`MarkerSource` on this checker rather than ship a second bead-aware
expiry linter.
"""

